        "tos.text-unit.sid-5b2e03e4e5d0028ac9da4b55089941d8"
      ],
      "findings": [
        "IV.01 says that Zarathustra squanders what is given him, and separately names honey and his happiness as bait for people. It does not identify the happiness cast as bait with an acquired gift or say that the act of spending what was given has this purpose. Compare liberation from purpose in III.04 with declared intent of the bait, without identifying the bait with a received gift."
      ]
